@startuml
title Grant lifecycle — Active, Revoked, and the UTC-epoch-day counter roll
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #ECF5FC
  BorderColor #477B9B
  StartColor #2F7C5A
  EndColor #7D478F
  ArrowColor #496174
}

state "Active" as active #E9F5EA {
  state "runs_today = {day: d, count: c}" as counter #FFF0D9
  counter : same day, c < cap  -> admit, c := c + 1
  counter : same day, c >= cap -> abort "grant daily run cap exhausted"
  counter : new day, cap > 0   -> admit, d := d(t), c := 1
  counter : cap absent (Nil)   -> admit, counter untouched
}
state "Revoked" as revoked #F8DADA

[*] --> active : createGrant (grantor-signed;\ngrantor derived from the deploy's signer;\nrevoked: false, runs_today {day 0, count 0})
active --> active : createGrant with the same grant_id\nand identical fields -- idempotent re-ack;\nany field differing aborts "grant identity conflict"
active --> active : beginDurableRunUnderGrant admitted\n(counter transition inside)
active --> revoked : revokeGrant (grantor-only;\nany other signer aborts\n"grant revocation requires the grantor")
revoked --> revoked : revokeGrant again --\nidempotent re-acknowledgment
revoked --> revoked : beginDurableRunUnderGrant\naborts "grant is revoked";\ngrantee reveal / command claims abort

note right of active #FFF6C9
Day window: <latex>d(t) = \lfloor t / 86\,400\,000 \rfloor</latex>
over the deploy's own node-validated timestamp
(milliseconds). O(1) counter state; up to
<latex>2\times</latex> the cap can land across one midnight
boundary (yesterday's remainder plus today's
fresh window). The cap is an abuse throttle,
not an invariant.
end note

note right of revoked #FFF0C7
Revocation is DELIVERY-ONLY for in-flight runs:
the run completes for its owner; the grantee's
reveal and command claims fail from the moment
of revocation; the owner keeps cancel through
the ordinary command envelope. The record is
never deleted -- a public audit fact, flagged
in every listing.
end note

note bottom of active #FFF0C7
Idempotent resend never double-counts: a re-registered
run_id verifies its identity and acknowledges without
touching runs_today (the same-signed envelope carries
the same deploy identity anyway).
end note
@enduml
